# Selenium → Playwright Migration Blueprint — Part 1
# CURRENT ARCHITECTURE ANALYSIS

> **Project**: QA Agent — AI-Powered Autonomous Testing Platform  
> **Scope**: Complete Selenium → Playwright migration  
> **Author**: Principal Architecture Review  
> **Date**: 2026-05-17

---

## 1.1 System Overview

The QA Agent is an AI-powered autonomous testing platform with the following core components:

| Layer | Technology | Role |
|-------|-----------|------|
| Frontend | React + Vite | SPA with real-time WebSocket updates |
| Backend API | FastAPI (ASGI) | REST + WebSocket gateway |
| Agent Orchestrator | LangGraph (StateGraph) | Autonomous workflow: analyze → plan → script → execute → fix → report |
| LLM Provider | Groq (Llama 3.3 70B) | Test case generation, script generation, self-healing |
| RAG Pipeline | Pinecone + SentenceTransformers | Context retrieval for grounded test generation |
| Browser Automation | Selenium + ChromeDriver | Script execution via subprocess |
| Artifact Capture | OpenCV + PIL | Video recording, screenshot capture |
| Persistence | Supabase (PostgreSQL + RLS) | Multi-tenant data with row-level security |
| Scheduling | APScheduler | Cron-based test scheduling |
| Real-time | python-socketio | WebSocket streaming for execution events |

---

## 1.2 Execution Lifecycle

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User/Frontend
    participant API as FastAPI
    participant WS as WebSocket (Socket.IO)
    participant LG as LangGraph Workflow
    participant LLM as Groq LLM
    participant RAG as Pinecone RAG
    participant EX as Execution Service
    participant SUB as subprocess (Python)
    participant SEL as Selenium/ChromeDriver
    participant DB as Supabase

    U->>API: POST /api/autonomous/start
    API->>LG: asyncio.create_task(run_autonomous_mode)
    API-->>U: {status: "started"}

    LG->>LG: analyze_project(state)
    LG->>DB: Fetch project, HTML files, KB status
    LG->>RAG: Retrieve context chunks
    LG->>WS: emit_agent_log("Analyzing...")

    LG->>LG: create_test_plan(state)
    LG->>LLM: Generate test cases (run_in_executor)
    LG->>DB: Save test cases
    LG->>WS: emit_agent_log("Generated N test cases")

    LG->>LG: generate_scripts(state)
    loop For each test case
        LG->>LLM: generate_selenium_script (run_in_executor)
        LG->>DB: Save script to selenium_scripts table
    end
    LG->>WS: emit_agent_log("Ready with N scripts")

    LG->>LG: execute_tests(state)
    loop For each script
        LG->>EX: execute_test_script(script_content)
        EX->>SUB: subprocess.run([python, tmp_script.py])
        SUB->>SEL: Launch Chrome, execute steps
        SEL-->>SUB: stdout/stderr + exit code
        SUB-->>EX: ExecutionResult
        EX-->>LG: Result (status, duration, logs, artifacts)
    end

    LG->>LG: fix_failures(state) [Self-Healing]
    alt Has failures AND retry_count < 1
        LG->>LLM: Repair prompt with error context
        LG->>DB: Update script
        LG->>LG: Re-execute (loop back)
    end

    LG->>LG: generate_report(state)
    LG->>WS: emit_agent_log("Report compiled")
```

